{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Why a converter can’t just rebuild its children","anchor":"Why-a-converter-cant-just-rebuild-its-children","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The obvious "},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body — "},{"code":"self.chapters = domain.chapters.map { ChapterModel(from: $0) }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — is a row leak. A relationship’s "},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fires when the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"parent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is deleted, never when a child is dropped from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relationship, so the previously-related rows are detached rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removed: they stay in the store with no owner, and nothing ever collects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. Every save of the parent leaves another full copy of its children"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behind, the store grows for the life of the app, and "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only walks the current relationship — shows nothing wrong."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the write-back reconciles by "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead: rows whose identity survives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are updated in place, new identities are inserted, and identities that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gone are deleted outright."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Identity, not row identity","anchor":"Identity-not-row-identity","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciling in place also keeps "},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stable across a save."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That matters beyond tidiness: a rebuilt child is a delete plus an insert, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under CloudKit mirroring every parent edit re-uploads its whole subtree, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one of those writes a history transaction that a remote-change tick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then has to resolve."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Duplicates are kept, as everywhere else","anchor":"Duplicates-are-kept-as-everywhere-else","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" emits no "},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (CloudKit forbids unique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints), so several related rows may legitimately share one identity."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are all updated and all kept, matching "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": converging every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matching row is safe, while picking one survivor is not — two devices pick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different rows, each tombstones the other’s, and both are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0A13RelationCodecO","title":"SwiduxRelationCodec","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles a generated model’s "},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties against the domain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value being written. Not meant to be called directly."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-34utk","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-9zflx"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/swiduxrelationcodec"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","role":"symbol","title":"EntityDB","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A generic ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/